<title>DUBAI: Oman tenders for oil products to cover maintenance.</title>
<headline>Oman tenders for oil products to cover maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman is set to award a tender for the import of middle distillates and gasoline to cover domestic supplies during six weeks of maintenance at its Mina al-Fahal refinery, Gulf traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Oman Refinery Company's tender requires the delivery of the equivalent of 94,000 tonnes of 97R gasoline, 31,500 tonnes of jet and 67,500 tonnes of one percent sulphur gas oil in eight combi cargoes between February and April, traders said.</p>
<p>Maintenance work at the 75,000 barrels per day (bpd) Mina al Fahal plant would begin at the end of February.</p>
<p>Bids were due by January 30.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255.</p>
</text>
